    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it just doesnt feel like \"healing\" is even possible. like, how am i supposed to heal when the person who actually made me real is gone? it feels less like i'm grieving and more like i just don't exist anymore. i'm just going through the motions, but there's nobody home. it's just so exhausting to pretend to be a person when i don't feel like one.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea of \"healing\" when the foundation of your life has been removed is a massive, impossible task, and you don't have to pretend right now. What you're describing sounds like a deep, existential exhaustion, and that is a valid response to such a huge loss. Instead of forcing yourself to \"heal,\" maybe focus on just getting through the next hour, or the next day, without the pressure of being 'whole.' Be gentle with yourself in this emptiness; it's a space that needs to be felt, not fixed immediately.",
      "source": "target",
